a,y,u∈E. H functions live on E×E modulo J-AE. Kernel reflection and density equalities hold for every y. Class pullback and g/Ag representatives hold only J-AE. Derivative and gradient assertions concern the literal Bochner-integral function Tf.","constant_dependencies":"P is fixed by E,V,η and J. R,S may depend on the initial data but are chosen before all y, U and f. U is chosen after the common kernels and before all f. g is chosen separately after each admissible f. The energy constant depends explicitly on α,η; β imposes a hypothesis.","source_text_visible":false,"source_identity_sought":false,"source_fidelity_verdict":null,"prior_mathematical_exposure":false,"compiler_started":false,"actual_inputs":[{"path":"E:/Samplinglib/.astis/decoder-50/packet0.json","raw_sha256":"28357bfe2bcf8a31221dbd43b3b774e171fbedeb056e6130e1f7f18047de587f","lf_sha256":"02a5af462d61041b94909d020efbc3b11fafb82385acdc4ed66de2dbeb5e3c27","bytes":6790},{"path":"E:/Samplinglib/.astis/decoder-50/lease.json","raw_sha256":"b51177c31059dc94022abcc79720a3ccacf7c29853433ad4d20f2c4701b84d51","lf_sha256":"436f577edb650a353d29db789fe9ff9504dcd873165eee2ace37c6d9176e1b92","bytes":685}],"decoder_run_sha256":"42ed953d61197c87c06ba038bb1d696db462759fd971f417dac580b111e8c146"}